{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Chart 15 — Venue density under the network, inner Melbourne. The zoomed synthesis: venues are binned offline into a hexagonal tessellation (venue_hexbins_melbourne.topojson, built by tools/build-hexbins.mjs from venues_web.csv over the same Melbourne frame, lon 144.75–145.35 / lat −37.92 to −37.67) and drawn as projected hexagons underneath the train + tram routes. Small train/tram stop dots sit over the route lines, making the network read as a sequence of stopping points without plotting the bus-stop cloud. A true hexbin tiles seamlessly and stays aligned with the route layer at any width, which fixed-size circles or point-mark hexagons cannot. The message: venue concentration piles up along the tram grid and radial train lines, instead of only identifying Melbourne on a statewide grid. Proximity, not service. Data: venue_hexbins_melbourne.topojson over pt_routes_melbourne.topojson, transport_stops_web.csv filtered to the Melbourne frame, and sa2_melbourne.topojson.",
  "title": {
    "text": "Venue density hugs the network — inner Melbourne",
    "subtitle": [
      "Each hex ≈ 1 km² · train and tram routes overlaid · venue count drives hex colour."
    ],
    "anchor": "start",
    "subtitleFontStyle": "italic"
  },
  "width": "container",
  "height": 520,
  "autosize": {
    "type": "fit-x",
    "contains": "padding"
  },
  "projection": {
    "type": "conicEqualArea",
    "rotate": [-145, 0, 0],
    "center": [0, -37],
    "parallels": [-36, -38]
  },
  "layer": [
    {
      "description": "Base: inner-Melbourne SA2 boundaries (shared clipped base).",
      "data": {
        "url": "data/sa2_melbourne.topojson",
        "format": {
          "type": "topojson",
          "feature": "sa2_summary"
        }
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "geoshape",
        "fill": "#f4f3ee",
        "stroke": "#ffffff",
        "strokeWidth": 0.4
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Venue density as a hexagonal tessellation, binned offline from venues_web.csv (tools/build-hexbins.mjs) so the cells are real geographic polygons that tile seamlessly. The venue count per hex is encoded by a single sequential warm fill — size is fixed because the cells tile, so this is colour-only, no size channel.",
      "data": {
        "url": "data/venue_hexbins_melbourne.topojson",
        "format": {
          "type": "topojson",
          "feature": "venue_hexbins"
        }
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "calculate": "datum.properties.count < 5 ? '<5' : datum.properties.count < 20 ? '5-20' : datum.properties.count < 100 ? '20-100' : '100+'",
          "as": "count_band"
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "geoshape",
        "stroke": "#ffffff",
        "strokeWidth": 0.3
      },
      "encoding": {
        "color": {
          "field": "count_band",
          "type": "ordinal",
          "title": "Venues per hex cell",
          "scale": {
            "domain": ["<5", "5-20", "20-100", "100+"],
            "range": ["#bdbdbd", "#fed976", "#e31a1c", "#800026"]
          },
          "legend": {
            "orient": "bottom",
            "direction": "horizontal",
            "columns": 4,
            "symbolType": "square",
            "symbolSize": 100
          }
        },
        "tooltip": [
          {
            "field": "properties.count",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Venues in hex",
            "format": ","
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Train + tram routes, Melbourne-clipped, drawn on top of the binned venue-density layer so the public-transport representation is the visible overlay.",
      "data": {
        "url": "data/pt_routes_melbourne.topojson",
        "format": {
          "type": "topojson",
          "feature": "public_transport_lines"
        }
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "calculate": "indexof(datum.properties.MODE, 'TRAIN') >= 0 ? 'Train' : 'Tram'",
          "as": "route_group"
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "geoshape",
        "filled": false,
        "strokeWidth": 1.5,
        "strokeCap": "round",
        "interactive": false
      },
      "encoding": {
        "color": {
          "field": "route_group",
          "type": "nominal",
          "title": "Routes (train & tram)",
          "scale": {
            "domain": ["Train", "Tram"],
            "range": ["#26384f", "#657385"]
          },
          "legend": {
            "symbolType": "stroke",
            "symbolStrokeWidth": 2,
            "orient": "bottom",
            "direction": "horizontal"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Train/tram stops in the inner-Melbourne frame. The dots sit on top of the route strokes to show where the visible lines actually stop, while excluding bus stops to avoid visual noise.",
      "data": {
        "url": "data/transport_stops_web.csv"
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "filter": "(indexof(datum.MODE, 'TRAIN') >= 0 || indexof(datum.MODE, 'TRAM') >= 0) && datum.Longitude >= 144.75 && datum.Longitude <= 145.35 && datum.Latitude >= -37.92 && datum.Latitude <= -37.67"
        },
        {
          "calculate": "'Train/tram stops'",
          "as": "stop_layer"
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "circle",
        "size": 13,
        "filled": true,
        "stroke": "#26384f",
        "strokeWidth": 0.55,
        "opacity": 0.95,
        "interactive": false
      },
      "encoding": {
        "longitude": {
          "field": "Longitude",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "latitude": {
          "field": "Latitude",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "color": {
          "field": "stop_layer",
          "type": "nominal",
          "title": "Stops",
          "scale": {
            "domain": ["Train/tram stops"],
            "range": ["#f8f7f1"]
          },
          "legend": {
            "orient": "bottom",
            "direction": "horizontal",
            "symbolType": "circle",
            "symbolSize": 90,
            "symbolStrokeColor": "#26384f",
            "symbolStrokeWidth": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "In-chart proximity clarification badge — reinforces that the map shows walking distance to stops, not service frequency.",
      "data": {
        "values": [{}]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "left",
        "baseline": "bottom",
        "fontSize": 10,
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "color": "#666",
        "x": {
          "expr": "8"
        },
        "y": {
          "expr": "height - 8"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "resolve": {
    "scale": {
      "color": "independent"
    }
  }
}
